From b7d5504c93ece7fdf73571f6252522d07fcc7e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:33:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 80/97] Input: PC keyboard typing + Ctrl+V paste for titles'
 text entry

- MnK: typed characters (OnKeyChar) become VK_PACKET+unicode keystrokes for titles that read
  XamInputGetKeystroke; Ctrl+V reads the clipboard (new rex::ui::GetClipboardText, Win32 + GTK).
- TextEntryTarget hook (rex::input): a title can register a pad-driven on-screen keyboard; while it
  is active, MnK stops mapping printable keys to pad buttons and types each queued character by
  calling SelectChar() and pulsing A (50 ms down / 50 ms up); Space=Y, Backspace=X, Enter=Start,
  Escape=B.
- InputSystem::GetKeystroke polls every driver (an EMPTY gamepad no longer hides MnK keystrokes).
- Default-off --debug_keystroke_poll_log counter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
